# Model roles

Default models for Task/subagent work (unless the user overrides in-session with a **non-Fast** model):

| Role | Model | Slug |
|------|--------|------|
| Explore / research | Composer 2.5 | `composer-2.5` |
| Coding / implementation | Grok 4.5 High | `cursor-grok-4.5-high` |

- **MUST** always set `model` explicitly when launching Task/subagents. Pass the appropriate non-Fast slug from the table (or the user's non-Fast override). **Do not omit `model`** and rely on parent inheritance.
- **Never ever** use Fast variants of any model — no exceptions. This includes `composer-2.5-fast`, `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`, and any other slug ending in `-fast` or labeled "Fast". **Do not use Fast variants even if the user explicitly requests them**, or if the Task tool only lists a Fast slug — use the non-Fast equivalent / coding default instead.
- If the user names a different **non-Fast** model for a task in-session, honor that override for that session/task.
- Parent/coordinator turns use the same defaults when spawning those roles.
